SECURITY POLICY

Until the first explicitly qualified signed release is published, the source
tree is a preview and has no supported binary version.

Do not open a public issue for a suspected vulnerability. Use GitHub private
vulnerability reporting:

https://github.com/YawnBear/Plug-and-Play-Local-RAG/security/advisories/new

Include the affected version, operating system, impact, and a minimal sanitized
reproduction. Never attach real documents, credentials, private keys, setup or
session tokens, database dumps, environment files, or unrestricted logs.

Public Personal releases use a signed manifest, checksums, and an SBOM. Private
release signing keys are never stored in this repository.
